    <DataNode elementId="AT4G02780-MONOMER" textLabel="ent-copalyl pyrophosphate synthase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q38802" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana ga1&lt;/i&gt; mutants are male-sterile dwarfs whose mutant phenotypes can be restored by application of exogenous gibberellin (GA). These mutants contain reduced levels of GAs and the &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-kaurene synthase activity in cell-free preparations from &lt;i&gt;ga1&lt;/i&gt; mutants is very low compared to wild-type. The functional study of the &lt;i&gt;CPS&lt;/i&gt; (&lt;i&gt;GA1&lt;/i&gt;) demonstrated that the protein encoded by this gene has &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-kaurene synthase A activity, which is responsible for the conversion of geranylgeranyl diphosphate (GGPP) into &lt;i&gt;ent&lt;/i&gt;-kaurene biosynthesis intermediate: copalyl diphosphate (CPP) |CITS:[7994182]|. The gene was expressed in &lt;i&gt;E.coli&lt;/i&gt; where it was shown to convert GGPP into CPP.</Comment>
